// Test: cfunc-missing
// Purpose: a call to a C function the host cannot resolve is an error, not a
//          value. `cov` is a lazy dylib module (lib/cov.c) with no .ta glue:
//          cov.nosuchop dlopens the module fine, then the *symbol* misses —
//          the permissive dotted-call path must name the symbol and the
//          module and exit 1 (issue #203). (`str`/`file` were the original
//          subjects, but they are now lazy dylibs with .ta lift layers — a
//          str.*/file.* miss is caught at typecheck as a not-exported error,
//          so it no longer reaches this runtime path; `cov` still does.)
//          stderr asserted by run_crash_tests.sh; stdout must stay empty.
fn main() {
  let r = cov.nosuchop(1)
  print("unreachable")
}
